xv6 is a re-implementation of Dennis Ritchie's and Ken Thompson's Unix Version 6 (v6). It loosely follows the structure and style of the original v6 while being implemented in ANSI C for a modern RISC-V multiprocessor.

Acknowledgments
xv6 is inspired by John Lions's Commentary on UNIX 6th Edition (Peer to Peer Communications; ISBN: 1-57398-013-7; 1st edition, June 14, 2000).

For additional information and online resources related to Version 6 Unix, visit:

https://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.1810/

