Error Reports
Please send errors and suggestions to Frans Kaashoek and Robert Morris (kaashoek,rtm@mit.edu).

Since xv6 is primarily intended as a teaching operating system for MIT's 6.1810 course, improvements that simplify or clarify the system are generally preferred over adding new features.

Building and Running xv6
Before building xv6, install the following:

A RISC-V newlib toolchain from:
https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain
QEMU built with riscv64-softmmu support.
After both tools are installed and available in your shell's PATH, start xv6 by running:
make qemu
